diff --git a/AGENTS.md b/AGENTS.md
index 12b2c86..3870b72 100644
--- a/AGENTS.md
+++ b/AGENTS.md
@@ -34,6 +34,8 @@ Dev-only environment variables (see `capture.go`, `app/app.go`, `app/session.go`
 - `BAIDUNETGO_CAPTURE=out.png` (with `BAIDUNETGO_CAPTURE_AFTER=4s`): write a PNG of the window, then quit. This is how to look at the real window from a script.
 - `BAIDUNETGO_SELFTEST=report.json` (`selftest.go`, `internal/selftest`): headless run of every feature against the saved session, else BaiduPCS-Go's login, inside a `/BaiduNetGo自检-…` folder it deletes afterwards. `BAIDUNETGO_PROBE=1` adds the download speed probe.
 - `BAIDUNETGO_SNAPSHOTS=dir` with `go test ./app`: tests that call `save(t, tt, name)` write `ui.Tester.Image()` PNGs there, for visual checks without a window.
+- `BAIDUNETGO_FONT=family`: override the interface font family; empty leaves the setting alone, `-` forces MyGo's own system font.
+- `BAIDUNETGO_FONT_SIZE=dip`: override the interface font size in DIP (an integer).
 
 ## Architecture
 
@@ -41,6 +43,8 @@ Dev-only environment variables (see `capture.go`, `app/app.go`, `app/session.go`
 
 **Phases and routing.** `App.phase` is booting → login → ready. Once ready, `shell.go` draws the sidebar and title bar around a `ui.Router` with these routes: `/files/{path...}` (netdisk path, segments `url.PathEscape`d by `filesRoute`/`dirOfRoute`), `/search?q=`, `/transfers`, `/shares`, `/offline`, `/dedup`, `/recycle`, `/settings`. The title bar's controls switch on `a.section()`. Each directory gets its own `listing` (cached in `a.listings`, keyed by dir), so a page sliding out during a router transition keeps showing its own files.
 
+**Interface font (`internal/fontconfig`).** The interface follows this computer's fontconfig default sans-serif rather than a hard-coded face, which matters on desktops without XSettings where MyGo finds no GTK interface font. `fontconfig.Family`/`Size`/`Detected` run `fc-match -f "%{family[0]}\n%{size}\n" sans-serif` once with a 500 ms timeout and cache the answer (`sync.Once`), dropping empty and placeholder families; non-Linux builds return empty so MyGo keeps its own system font. `App.resolvedFont` turns the point size into DIP (`round(pt*4/3)`, clamped 11–17), and `App.applyTheme` sets the light/dark `ui.Theme`'s `Font`/`FontSize` from it each frame. `settings.FollowSystemFont` (nil, so true, by default) turns it off to the built-in 13 DIP and empty family; `BAIDUNETGO_FONT` and `BAIDUNETGO_FONT_SIZE` override both for tests and as an escape hatch. The settings page's 外观 section shows the detected face and a switch. A failed detection or no fontconfig is silent: the app keeps the built-in font.
+
 **Overlays.** One `a.dlg` (`dialog` with a `dialogKind`) drives every modal through `a.dialogs`. The file preview is a separate overlay (`a.pv`, `previewOverlay`). The image preview and the grid/list thumbnails share `ui.ElementTransition{Match: thumbMatch{fsid}}`. The source thumbnail is skipped while `a.previewing(f)`, so the image grows out of it and shrinks back.
 
 **File clipboard and shortcuts.** The browser's keys are handled in `app/ops.go`'s `fileActions` once per `filesPage` frame, yielding while a dialog, the preview, a rename or a folder being named is open. Cmd-C/X put the chosen files in `a.fileClip` (`app/fileclip.go`), an in-memory `fileClipboard{files, from, cut, cutSet, gen}` — never the system clipboard, as a netdisk path means nothing elsewhere. A cut fills `cutSet` by path, so a row's `isCut` says in constant time whether it shows the `待移动` chip; `putFiles` bumps `App.fileClipGen`, and sign-out clears the clipboard. Cmd-V pastes that clipboard through the picker's `place`/`moveOrCopyAfter`, which asks about names a folder has exactly as `复制到…` does; only when the file clipboard is empty does it fall back to `openClipboardShare`, the share-link behavior it had before, while Cmd-Shift-V always opens a share link. Pasting runs on goroutines through `a.run`, and the `after` callback runs only when the netdisk operation succeeded: a cut then clears the clipboard only if `fileClip.gen` is still the one it pasted, so a cut made while the first is moving survives. Cmd-Shift-C copies paths to the system clipboard, Cmd-A selects every non-temporary row in both views, and F5 refreshes as Cmd-R does. A held key acts once: auto-repeats of these file keys are ignored, and while an operation is busy the browser takes no file key, so a paste cannot start twice.
@@ -86,7 +90,7 @@ Entering the page reads the cache again only when it is entered (`dedupEnter` no
 - Virtualized `List` rows get no enter/exit transitions. Staggered entrances use `Keyframes` inside the row (`entering` in `browser.go`).
 - The grid view is not `ui.GridView`: GridView builds each line as an element, so a tile that a resize moves to another line is built anew and jumps. `app/grid.go` positions tiles itself, all under one parent keyed by fsid (percent `Left`/`Width`, so the width never lags), and on a cell change `Jump`s the slot's offset to where it showed and `AnimateTo`s it back to 0. Element `Transition`s don't help here: MyGo skips layout transitions on frames where the window resized.
 - The folder's actions live in a toolbar on the path bar (`app/browser.go`'s `filesToolbar`): a new folder (`folder-plus`), the sort menu, the view switch, the clipboard-link button, refresh, and the upload pill at the end; the folder's own name and search sit before them, and the button's box is where a folder made from it flies from (`listing.makerAt`). The maker (`app/newfolder.go`) is no longer a place for buttons: the grid's last tile is a whole "新建" tile that makes a folder on a click (a plus, or an upload while files are dragged over the window, `listing.over`), and the list's maker row is only the drop hint, in the accent color saying where dropped files will go, built only while files are dragged so it takes no room at the foot of a full folder. An empty folder says "这里还空着" and offers one upload of its own, labelled apart from the toolbar's. A new folder is named in a draft row at the top (`draftID`, put back each frame by `placeDraft`); a click away with its name untouched gives up. Cmd-Shift-N starts it from the toolbar's button box.
-- Theme: the look is a native macOS app's, modeled on Pulse (egoist's MyGo app): the sidebar draws no background so the window's `VibrancySidebar` material shows (`main.go`: `TitleBarHiddenInset`, 52 px title bar), pages marked by white glyphs on colored tiles, the chosen one on a solid accent backdrop, a value at each row's end (`navValue`); the pane is white with a title over a subtitle (`pageTitle`), round gray tool buttons (`toolButton`), capsule segmented controls (`segmented`/`segmentedOf`), which fold into pop-up buttons (`choice`/`popUp`) when the title bar is narrower than `compactBar` (`a.compact`, from its last width; in a folder the tools fold instead whenever its whole path would not fit beside them open, `foldTools`, so the path never folds while they could give way, and the folder's title bar has no subtitle, the status bar counting its items), striped 28 px list rows (`stripe`), rounded gray `group` panels for settings and summaries, and the system typeface (no embedded fonts; `figure` sets tabular digits). Waits that fill a page or stand for a task use `plugins/loading` (a folder's `Ring`, the speed test's `Radar`; the boot screen shows no wait, only the bare window); small ones in buttons, rows and dialogs keep AppKit's `ui.Spinner`. `applyTheme` swaps in the app's light/dark `ui.Theme` each frame. Extra colors are in `palette`. Motion is one curve and three lengths (`motionHover` 120 ms, `motionFade` 160 ms, `motionPanel` 180 ms), plus `popIn` and `rowEnter`, all in `app/theme.go`; no springs or bounce.
+- Theme: the look is a native macOS app's, modeled on Pulse (egoist's MyGo app): the sidebar draws no background so the window's `VibrancySidebar` material shows (`main.go`: `TitleBarHiddenInset`, 52 px title bar), pages marked by white glyphs on colored tiles, the chosen one on a solid accent backdrop, a value at each row's end (`navValue`); the pane is white with a title over a subtitle (`pageTitle`), round gray tool buttons (`toolButton`), capsule segmented controls (`segmented`/`segmentedOf`), which fold into pop-up buttons (`choice`/`popUp`) when the title bar is narrower than `compactBar` (`a.compact`, from its last width; in a folder the tools fold instead whenever its whole path would not fit beside them open, `foldTools`, so the path never folds while they could give way, and the folder's title bar has no subtitle, the status bar counting its items), striped 28 px list rows (`stripe`), rounded gray `group` panels for settings and summaries, and the system typeface (no embedded fonts; `figure` sets tabular digits). Waits that fill a page or stand for a task use `plugins/loading` (a folder's `Ring`, the speed test's `Radar`; the boot screen shows no wait, only the bare window); small ones in buttons, rows and dialogs keep AppKit's `ui.Spinner`. `applyTheme` swaps in the app's light/dark `ui.Theme` each frame, its interface font coming from `internal/fontconfig` (see above). Extra colors are in `palette`. Motion is one curve and three lengths (`motionHover` 120 ms, `motionFade` 160 ms, `motionPanel` 180 ms), plus `popIn` and `rowEnter`, all in `app/theme.go`; no springs or bounce.
 - Shaders (`ui/shader`, sources in `app/shaders/*.kage`, wiring in `app/effects.go`): each shader draw, effect layer or gradient with stops is a "general" GPU instance that the window does not batch, so dozens of them cost frames. Measure with `MYGO_FRAME_STATS=all` (it counts instances by class); draw many small things as plain fills, and keep a shader's per-pixel loop short (`specks.kage` searches only the cells whose specks can reach the pixel, from one hash each, and returns at once outside their reach). Shaders and `Element.Effect` run interpreted on the CPU in `ui.Tester`, so the app uses them only when `a.gpu` (`p.Accelerated()`), with plain fallbacks the tests see.
 - `Painter.AnimationFrame` (and `After`) only paints the window again: the view is not built, so anything computed while building (an element's size, an effect's uniforms, state moved on in `View`) stands still in those frames. Read the time as you paint (`p.Now()` in a `Draw` callback, or in an effect's `PaintEffect`, as `specksFx` does), and call `c.Invalidate()` while something built must move (`a.moving()`). Stamp an animation's start in the first frame that shows it, not from the last frame built, which may be long past.
 - Files come and go through specks (`app/arrivals.go`): a deleted file stays in its listing while it dissolves (`a.dying`, kept through reloads by `keepDying`), and an upload shows in its folder at once as a row with a negative FsID that gathers as its bytes go up (`a.gathers`, by the path of the entry it makes); rows with a negative FsID or dissolving are never chosen or opened.
diff --git a/CHANGELOG.md b/CHANGELOG.md
index a8ac894..bbf731f 100644
--- a/CHANGELOG.md
+++ b/CHANGELOG.md
@@ -6,6 +6,7 @@
 
 ### 新增
 
+- 界面字体族与字号新增「跟随本机 fontconfig」：默认读取 `fc-match sans-serif` 解析出的字体（字号按 1pt ≈ 4/3 DIP 换算并限幅 11–17），可在设置页「外观」里关闭改用内置字体；`BAIDUNETGO_FONT` / `BAIDUNETGO_FONT_SIZE` 可临时覆盖，没有 fontconfig 时静默回落。
 - 查重结果行新增右键菜单：打开预览（同一重复组的图片可在预览里用左右键翻页）、在文件夹中显示、复制路径。
 - 查重：按网盘 MD5 与文件大小，在整个网盘或选定文件夹中递归比对；按可释放空间分组展示，默认每组保留修改时间最早的一份，可全选 / 全不选后批量移入回收站；缺少 MD5 的文件会跳过并注明。删除前会重新读取所在目录，核对 fs_id、大小和 MD5，并确保每组仍留有一份，过期或被替换的文件不会误删。
 - 文件浏览器新增剪切 / 复制 / 粘贴（Cmd+X / Cmd+C / Cmd+V）：文件剪贴板只在应用内，跨文件夹移动或复制沿用“复制到…”的同名冲突处理（跳过 / 替换 / 保留两者）；剪切成功后才清空剪贴板，失败、取消或全部跳过时保留可重试，复制则可连续粘贴；剪切到原文件夹、把文件夹粘进自身或子目录会被拒绝，注销时清空。另有 Cmd+A 全选、Cmd+Shift+C 复制网盘路径、Cmd+Shift+V 始终打开系统剪贴板里的分享链接（Cmd+V 在文件剪贴板为空时才这么做）、F5 刷新；右键菜单与状态栏显示剪贴板状态，被剪切的行标出“待移动”，README 增补了快捷键说明。
