+// Package fontconfig reads the desktop's default sans-serif font from
+// fontconfig, which on Linux is what the rest of the desktop draws with.
+// MyGo only asks GTK for its gtk-font-name and takes no size, so on a
+// desktop without XSettings (Hyprland, for one) it finds nothing and
+// falls back to a built-in face; this package gives the app the face
+// fontconfig itself resolves for sans-serif.
+//
+// Detection runs once and is cached. On a platform without fontconfig,
+// and when fc-match is missing, fails or prints nothing usable, the
+// functions return empty results and the caller keeps its own font.
+package fontconfig
